

Name: The Strand 
By: Jaxson Character, Brennan Howard-Ruelas, Diego Ortega Gonzales






It sees: your prototype's real numbers for nobody, a little and a lot, from its README or three fresh Serial Monitor readings. A PIR reads only 0 or 1023 in the Wire Any Sensor sketch, so its numbers are seconds of motion.
Nobody: if nobody is in the range it says no object 
Close: it says close (0,15)cm 
Far: (15,infinity)cm 
It calls you: one name per member of your group, plus one for nobody. Each name gets a number, which side of it, and a hold in seconds.
A PIR names by time: passing (motion under 5 s), lingering (motion for 5 s), gone (nothing for 10 s).
A photoresistor is named by light: lit, shadowed, covered.
Nobody: 5 seconds  
Close: super close! 
Far: (15,infinity) cm 
It does: one action per name, no two the same, run by the Nano: an LED, the buzzer, a servo, the OLED.
Nobody: if nobody is in the range it says no object 
Close: it says close (0,15)cm 
Far: (15,infinity)cm 
For them and To them: one line each: what the piece does for the person, and what it does to them.
For them: it gives visitors an experience that responds to their physical presence 
To them: makes them feel like their presence makes a difference 
It refuses: one thing it could do with what it knows, and will not.
It doesn't record their moments or remember anything, it just responds to their distance in the current moment. 
Reminds me of: one entry from the References page.
	It reminds me of the radar sensor in my car where AEB works because that measures distance constantly. 




